---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms"
  description="Don't use Gridwatch to guess future electricity prices, or to make decisions about the energy market or how it is run. Gridwatch can get things wrong."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Terms</h1>
    <div class="split" role="group" aria-label="What this data is for">
      <div class="ok">
        <p class="label">Use this for</p>
        <p>Looking at a day that has already finished.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="no">
        <p class="label">Don't use this for</p>
        <p>
          Guessing future prices, or making decisions about the energy market
          or how it is run.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <h2>Forecasting</h2>
    <p>
      Don't use this data for forecasting. Forecasting means guessing what
      electricity prices will do next, or how much power the country will use
      or make. Gridwatch looks at what already happened.
    </p>
    <h2>Market and operations</h2>
    <p>
      Don't use this site's numbers to make decisions about the energy market
      or its operations. Operations means how the market is run from day to
      day.
    </p>
    <p>
      Gridwatch is independent. It isn't the Electricity Authority, the
      government body that sets the rules for the electricity market, and it
      isn't the grid operator, the people who keep the lights on.
    </p>
    <p>
      The numbers come from EMI, the Authority's public electricity data, and
      Gridwatch can still get things wrong. If you need an official figure,
      get it from EMI.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  @media (min-width: 40rem) {
    .split {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  .split > div {
    background: var(--color-card);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .ok {
    box-shadow: inset 0 4px 0 var(--color-brand);
  }

  .no {
    box-shadow: inset 0 4px 0 var(--color-caution);
  }

  .label {
    font-size: var(--text-label);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
</style>
